[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4183577850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118155#issuecomment-4183577850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118155","id":4183577850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75XFT6","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-03T13:54:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T14:20:25Z","body":"> Doing the filtering in `_body_motion_cast` is not strictly related to the above mentioned issue, but seems like the right thing to do. It might be a bad idea.\r\n\r\nJust to have it said out loud, one thing that might make this particular change questionable is the fact that the margin parameter (not to be confused with Godot's shape margins) that's passed into `body_test_motion`, which is normally 1 mm and at least 0.1 mm, is applied to the recovery step as well as the collision step, but not during the cast step.\r\n\r\nI don't know if I ever understood the true purpose of this margin, nor if it's even being utilized properly here, but one apparent consequence of it is that it adds a bit of \"play\" for the cast, allowing 